        Publications are not static items in a hardcoded grid. In Fundamental Engine, each publication is a
        <strong>Field Body</strong> carrying relevance mass and citation graph edges. Category containers act as
        <strong>Attractor Wells</strong> that pull matching papers into spatial topology, while live CSS variables
        (<code>--field-density</code>, <code>--field-proximity</code>, <code>--field-tension</code>) drive glassmorphic elevation, border glow, and visual formatting without JS event overhead.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Controls & Category Filters -->
